--
308-
309-        > Generation parameters exclusive to assistant generation
310-        is_assistant (`bool`):
311-            Whether the model is an assistant (draft) model.
312:        num_assistant_tokens (`int`, *optional*):
313-            Defines the number of _speculative tokens_ that shall be generated by the assistant model before being
314:            checked by the target model at each iteration. Higher values for `num_assistant_tokens` make the generation
315-            more _speculative_ : If the assistant model is performant larger speed-ups can be reached, if the assistant
316-            model requires lots of corrections, lower speed-ups are reached.
317:        num_assistant_tokens_schedule (`str`, *optional*):
318-            Defines the schedule at which max assistant tokens shall be changed during inference.
319:            - `"heuristic"`: When all speculative tokens are correct, increase `num_assistant_tokens` by 2 else
320:              reduce by 1. `num_assistant_tokens` value is persistent over multiple generation calls with the same assistant model.
321:            - `"heuristic_transient"`: Same as `"heuristic"` but `num_assistant_tokens` is reset to its initial value after each generation call.
322:            - `"constant"`: `num_assistant_tokens` stays unchanged during generation
323:        assistant_confidence_threshold (`float`, *optional*):
324-            The confidence threshold for the assistant model. If the assistant model's confidence in its prediction for the current token is lower
325-            than this threshold, the assistant model stops the current token generation iteration, even if the number of _speculative tokens_
326:            (defined by `num_assistant_tokens`) is not yet reached. The assistant's confidence threshold is adjusted throughout the speculative iterations to reduce the number of unnecessary draft and target forward passes, biased towards avoiding false negatives.
327:            `assistant_confidence_threshold` value is persistent over multiple generation calls with the same assistant model.
328-            It is an unsupervised version of the dynamic speculation lookahead
329-            from Dynamic Speculation Lookahead Accelerates Speculative Decoding of Large Language Models <https://huggingface.co/papers/2405.04304>.
330-        prompt_lookup_num_tokens (`int`, *optional*):
331-            The number of tokens to be output as candidate tokens.
332-        max_matching_ngram_size (`int`, *optional*):
333-            The maximum ngram size to be considered for matching in the prompt. Default to 2 if not provided.
334-        assistant_early_exit(`int`, *optional*):
335-            If set to a positive integer, early exit of the model will be used as an assistant. Can only be used with
336-            models that support early exit (i.e. models where logits from intermediate layers can be interpreted by the LM head).
337-        assistant_lookbehind(`int`, *optional*):
338-            If set to a positive integer, the re-encodeing process will additionally consider the last `assistant_lookbehind` assistant tokens
339-            to correctly align tokens. Can only be used with different tokenizers in speculative decoding.
340-            See this [blog](https://huggingface.co/blog/universal_assisted_generation) for more details.
341-        target_lookbehind(`int`, *optional*):
342-            If set to a positive integer, the re-encodeing process will additionally consider the last `target_lookbehind` target tokens
343-            to correctly align tokens. Can only be used with different tokenizers in speculative decoding.
--
